    {
      "location": "Raw PDF page 25; printed page 3; opening paragraph",
      "anchor": "real eigenvalues and a corresponding set of m linearly independent eigenvectors",
      "observation": "Hyperbolicity of the constant-coefficient system means that A has real eigenvalues and a complete set of linearly independent eigenvectors. Every vector in R^m consequently has a unique expansion in this eigenvector basis. The eigenvalues give the propagation speeds of the corresponding waves."
    },
    {
      "location": "Raw PDF page 27; printed page 5; opening paragraph",
      "anchor": "does not hold in the classical sense",
      "observation": "At a discontinuity the differential conservation law need not hold classically; the text identifies the integral conservation law (1.10) as the more fundamental equation that continues to hold."
