      "location": "Raw PDF page 27; printed page 5; section 1.2.1 and equation (1.11)",
      "anchor": "piecewise constant with a single jump discontinuity",
      "observation": "A Riemann problem consists of the hyperbolic equation with initial data q(x,0) = q_l for x < 0 and q(x,0) = q_r for x > 0. The jump is placed at x = 0."
    },
    {
      "location": "Raw PDF page 27; printed page 5; paragraph following equation (1.11)",
      "anchor": "q_l = Q_{i−1} and q_r = Q_i",
      "observation": "Neighboring finite-volume cell averages can supply the two states. Solving this Riemann problem yields information usable to compute a numerical flux and update cell averages over a time step."
