      "location": "Raw PDF page 28; printed page 6; first two paragraphs",
      "anchor": "exact solution (or arbitrarily good approximations)",
      "observation": "The surrounding discussion extends the simple wave structure to nonlinear systems, gives the Euler equations as an example of constructing exact or arbitrarily accurate Riemann solutions, and explains the computational use of approximate Riemann solvers for nonlinear problems."
    }
